# User-level override of /usr/share/applications/firefox.desktop.
#
# Reason this file exists at all (2026-09-11): the previous copy here read
#   Exec=env GTK_CSD=0 GDK_BACKEND=x11 MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND= /usr/lib/firefox/firefox %u
# which forced Firefox onto XWayland and blanked the MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 that
# hyprland.lua already exports session-wide. mimeapps.list sends every
# http/https/html association to firefox.desktop, and a copy in
# ~/.local/share/applications shadows the one in /usr/share/applications, so
# every link opened from another application -- Slack, a mail client, anything
# going through xdg-open -- got the X11 environment, while typing `firefox` in a
# shell got the session default and came up as a native Wayland client. Same
# browser, two different graphics stacks depending on who launched it.
#
# The Exec below pins Wayland explicitly rather than relying on inheriting it,
# so the answer no longer depends on the launcher's environment.
#
# GTK_CSD=0 is deliberately NOT carried over. It belonged with the X11 choice
# (it tells GTK to skip client-side decorations and let the window manager draw
# them). Under Wayland, Hyprland draws the border itself and Firefox handles its
# own titlebar, and forcing CSD off there is a known way to end up with a window
# that has neither. Put it back only if something actually looks wrong.
#
# Two leftover "Custom definition for Firefox" entries, userapp-Firefox-DU5YU3
# and userapp-Firefox-T98QU3, forced X11 the same way. Nothing referenced them
# and both were NoDisplay=true. Moved to disabled-2026-09-11/ alongside the
# original of this file.
[Desktop Entry]
Encoding=UTF-8
Name=Firefox Web Browser
Comment=Browse the World Wide Web
GenericName=Web Browser
Exec=env MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 firefox %u
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Icon=firefox
Categories=GNOME;GTK;Network;WebBrowser;
MimeType=text/xml;text/mml;text/html;application/xhtml+xml;application/vnd.mozilla.xul+xml;x-scheme-handler/http;x-scheme-handler/https
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=firefox
